# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env
.env.local

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# Workflow / packaging scratch space
dist/
*.tar.gz
*.sha256
download-metadata.json

# Except the checksums under the served path: those are published artifacts and
# must be tracked, or `git add` in the publish job fails on them. The blanket
# *.sha256 above never bit before because the historical eden-memory-*.sha256
# files were already tracked and so bypassed it; the renamed paths are new.
#
# This pattern is coupled to the /memory/ DIRECTORY, which keeps its name because
# it is the served route — not to the artifact basenames. The publish job writes
# od3sa-memory-<os>-<arch>.sha256 here; do not "fix" this path when the asset
# basenames change.
!docs-site/public/memory/*.sha256

# Built binaries are published as GitHub Release assets only. Staging happens in
# binaries/ during a local or CI packaging run, so both binaries' artifact globs
# must be ignored; an uncovered glob leaves a 100 MB binary untracked-but-visible
# and one `git add binaries/` away from being committed.
binaries/od3sa-memory-*
binaries/od3sa-relay-*
!binaries/manifest.json

# Stale local ATP hand-off artifacts; the canonical hand-off records live in Memory.
.agentic-handoff/

# Impeccable skill local artifacts that are regenerated during design work.
.impeccable/config.local.json
.impeccable/direction-payload.json
.impeccable/hook.cache.json
.impeccable/screenshots/
.impeccable/sketches/

# Claude Code skill hook installed locally per session.
.github/hooks/impeccable.json

# Python caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Local tool state and npm artifacts (repo uses pnpm)
.pi/
docs-site/package-lock.json
